{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"tina4_code","description":"Generate Tina4 framework code, grounded on the live corpus. Give an `instruction`; it is grounded against the current Tina4 API and written by the large-context reader \u2014 no small fine-tune, so larger inputs and higher accuracy. `language` (python/php/js/nodejs/ruby) scopes the grounding; `image_url` turns a UI mockup/screenshot into code. (A capable agent can also just call `tina4_context` and write the code itself.)","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"instruction":{"type":"string"},"image_url":{"type":"string","default":""},"language":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["instruction"]}},{"name":"tina4_context","description":"RETRIEVAL-ONLY Tina4 grounding \u2014 returns the authoritative, version-current API + real examples for your request so YOU write the code. The recommended path for a capable agent: grounded on these exact imports/idioms a strong model writes runnable Tina4 code. (Want direct generation instead? tina4_code is an optional generator.) Pass `language` (python/php/js/nodejs/ruby).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"instruction":{"type":"string"},"language":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["instruction"]}},{"name":"long_context","description":"General large-context Q&A over whatever text you pass. Up to ~8 MB (~2,000,000 tokens / ~8,000,000 characters) PER CALL (MEASURED; larger returns HTTP 413); only retrieved chunks reach the reader, so its window is not the limit. NOT Tina4-specific. STACK PAST THE PER-CALL CAP: every response returns a `checksum` \u2014 pass it back as `checksum` on the next call to APPEND more `context` (returns a new checksum) or to RE-QUERY the stored context with no new `context` (same checksum). The accumulated corpus is unbounded; you only ever send the NEW chunk. Checksums are private to your token. Pass `context` and/or `checksum` (at least one).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"question":{"type":"string"},"context":{"type":"string","default":""},"checksum":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["question"]}},{"name":"tina4_image","description":"Generate an image (UI mockups, icons, assets, avatars). Returns one line of text: the PNG size and a public URL to fetch the image from. NOT inline base64 \u2014 that overflows the JSON-RPC result cap and fails the call. Pass `reference_image` (an http/https URL or a data: URI) to condition the generation on a reference \u2014 the result preserves that subject's identity and style (consistent avatars/characters across generations).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"prompt":{"type":"string"},"size":{"type":"string","default":"512x512"},"reference_image":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["prompt"]}},{"name":"describe_image","description":"Describe an image, or answer a question about it, using the gateway vision model. Pass `image_url` as an http/https URL or a data: URI. Returns a factual text description \u2014 layout, text, colours, UI elements, charts, content. Set `prompt` to ask something specific instead of a general description. This is image -> words; use tina4_image for words -> image, and tina4_code(image_url=...) to turn a mockup into Tina4 code.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"image_url":{"type":"string"},"prompt":{"type":"string","default":"Describe this image in detail."}},"required":["image_url"]}},{"name":"tina4_chat","description":"Multi-turn Tina4 chat, grounded on the live corpus. Pass the whole conversation as `messages` (OpenAI format: a list of {role, content}); the latest turn is grounded against the current Tina4 API and answered by the large-context reader, so long conversations and large pasted code/logs are fine. Optionally pass `language` (python/php/js/nodejs/ruby) to scope the grounding.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"messages":{"type":"array"},"language":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["messages"]}},{"name":"tina4_features","description":"List the Tina4 capabilities - the 97 built-in features with the canonical API/idiom PER LANGUAGE. Metadata only (no generation, no quota). Pass category (e.g. 'orm', 'auth') to filter, and/or language (python/php/js/nodejs/ruby) to get that language's idiom ('n/a' = the feature is not in that framework).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"category":{"type":"string","default":""},"language":{"type":"string","default":""}}}},{"name":"tina4_bug","description":"Report a Tina4 FRAMEWORK runtime bug \u2014 the framework itself misbehaves (not wrong generated code, which is a prompt/coder issue). Requires `language` (python/php/js/nodejs/ruby) and a MINIMAL, framework-only `repro` that triggers the bug using ONLY the framework, no app code \u2014 this is what proves it's a framework bug (not app misuse) and lets a maintainer reproduce it. Also give `title`, `description`, `expected`, `actual`, and `version`. Filed as a GitHub issue on the matching tina4stack repo when the server has an issue-filing token; otherwise the report is recorded and you get a pre-filled issue URL to open yourself.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"language":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"},"repro":{"type":"string"},"description":{"type":"string","default":""},"expected":{"type":"string","default":""},"actual":{"type":"string","default":""},"version":{"type":"string","default":""}},"required":["language","title","repro"]}},{"name":"tina4_delegate","description":"Delegate one bounded, low-risk task to the local Bonsai model so the calling agent can save its own generation tokens. Best for summaries, small functions, focused tests, symbol extraction, and mechanical transformations. This tool does NOT call tools, inspect files, or modify the workspace: pass only the relevant `context`, choose `output` as answer/patch/summary/tests, then verify the result yourself. Multi-step repository work and tool loops should stay with the calling agent.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string"},"context":{"type":"string","default":""},"language":{"type":"string","default":""},"output":{"type":"string","default":"answer"},"max_tokens":{"type":"integer","default":800}},"required":["task"]}},{"name":"web_search","description":"Find WHERE information is on the web \u2014 ranked results (title, url, snippet) from a self-hosted metasearch. This LOCATES pages; it does not read them. To read a result, follow up with fetch_page. Use it for current affairs, recent news, or a concrete factual question you do not already know \u2014 NOT for things answerable from your own knowledge. If the JSON has \"ok\": false the search FAILED (the internet could not be reached) \u2014 say so plainly and do NOT invent an answer in its place.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"max_results":{"type":"string","default":6}},"required":["query"]}},{"name":"fetch_page","description":"GO AND READ a web page \u2014 open it in a real headless browser (JavaScript runs, the page renders as a person sees it) and return its readable main content, stripped of navigation and ads. This is how you genuinely read the web: the article behind a search result, a news front page, a product page for a price. If the JSON has \"ok\": false the page could not be loaded; if it rendered but the text is thin, try screenshot_page instead.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"]}},{"name":"screenshot_page","description":"Open a web page in a real headless browser and capture a screenshot of the rendered page (PNG, base64). Use this when fetch_page returns little text, or when the page is visual \u2014 the image can be read by vision.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"]}}]},"signature":"\ud83c\udf8b Tina4 Thinker"}